# Story: Arbor seems to misbehave, so its owner switches it off under Privacy & Security → Accessibility, with two windows
# out of view. Arbor cannot fetch them. It stops pretending, says what happened and what to do, keeps its keys, so that
# pressing one leads somewhere and none lands in another app, and puts everything right when the switch goes back on.
# Written by the executor swarm (F63); for the documenter to review. Reference: A63.
open Safari
open Mail
open Notes
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
zoom 101
expect hidden 102
expect hidden 103
revoke
# Nobody tells Arbor. It asks every two seconds, and does not believe the first "no".
wait 3
# Commands fail, with the sentence; nothing is moved.
show-all
expect fail
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+space on
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+escape on
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+return on
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+left on
float-all
expect fail
toggle-pause
expect fail
# Queries still answer.
status
expect ok
# It takes a while to find the switch.
wait 20
grant
# Arbor asks once a second. Everything is in view, and the old view is one Back away.
wait 1
status
expect ok
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect visible 103
expect camera root
expect shortcut ctrl+opt+return on
back
expect camera 101
expect hidden 102
